cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research release, cite the immutable Zenodo version."
title: "SCILLA PASSIVE: Cue-Driven Opportunistic Maritime Verification Using Non-Cooperative Merchant-Radar Illumination"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Giletto"
    given-names: "Michele"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22229086"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22229086"
repository-code: "https://github.com/michelegiletto-beep/scilla-passive-evidence"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible simulation release evaluating cue-driven opportunistic passive
  maritime second observations using non-cooperative merchant-radar
  illumination. The released evidence supports a measurement-architecture
  hypothesis but does not demonstrate a donor-selection optimizer moat. No
  measured RF performance is claimed.
keywords:
  - "passive bistatic radar"
  - "maritime surveillance"
  - "illuminators of opportunity"
  - "commercial marine radar"
  - "opportunistic sensing"
  - "reproducible simulation"
  - "extended Kalman filter"
